        "description": "Resembles an IDOR / path-traversal file download: a DocumentVersion is fetched directly by a caller-supplied version_pk from the URL and streamed back via FileResponse using version.original_filename as the attachment name. It is actually safe: the view is @login_required and immediately calls can_access_document(request.user, version.document), which delegates to can_access_matter (enforcing attorney/paralegal/client tenant ownership) and additionally restricts CLIENT role to CLIENT_SHARED/PUBLIC_FILING visibility, raising PermissionDenied before any file is served. The filename is the stored model field, not raw user input, and FileResponse streams version.file (a managed FieldFile), not a path concatenated from request data."
